WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Sam: We reviewed eight education interviews.

2
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Iris: Six customers praised report export.

3
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Iris: Five could not find the setup guide.

4
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Sam: Did that block setup?

5
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Iris: No, support helped everyone finish.

6
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Iris: They expected in-product guidance.

7
00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Sam: Add a first-run checklist.

8
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Sam: Include invites, reports, and exports.

9
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:42.000
Iris: I will draft copy Thursday.

10
00:02:42.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Iris: Customer success will review it.

11
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Iris: Teachers use classes and terms.

12
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Sam: Test that language in templates.

13
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:54.000
Sam: Do not rename the whole product.

14
00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:12.000
Iris: Four customers wanted read-only sharing.

15
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Sam: Read-only links already exist.

16
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:48.000
Iris: They only knew PDF export.

17
00:04:48.000 --> 00:05:06.000
Sam: Improve sharing-menu clarity.

18
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Iris: Track sharing support tickets.

19
00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:42.000
Sam: Who owns the design?

20
00:05:42.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Iris: Design brings options Friday.

21
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:18.000
Iris: Pricing appeared twice.

22
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:36.000
Iris: Customers asked for annual invoicing.

23
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:54.000
Sam: Procurement cannot use monthly cards.

24
00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:12.000
Sam: Pricing will not change this quarter.

25
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Sam: Sales operations owns invoicing follow-up.

26
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:48.000
Iris: One export took almost a minute.

27
00:07:48.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Iris: The class had over 200 students.

28
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:24.000
Iris: Engineering has the account details.

29
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:42.000
Sam: It is not a release blocker yet.

30
00:08:42.000 --> 00:09:00.000
Sam: Engineering reports Friday.

31
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:18.000
Iris: Report templates received strong praise.

32
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:36.000
Iris: Duplicating reports saves time.

33
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Sam: Continue template investment.

34
00:09:54.000 --> 00:10:12.000
Sam: Any September template requests?

35
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:30.000
Iris: None have enough evidence.

36
00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:48.000
Sam: Commit checklist, sharing, and language test.

37
00:10:48.000 --> 00:11:06.000
Sam: Invoicing and performance are follow-ups.

38
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Iris: I will send timestamped interview clips.

39
00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:42.000
Iris: They cover setup and sharing.

40
00:11:42.000 --> 00:12:00.000
Sam: Checklist feedback is due Thursday.

41
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:18.000
Iris: I will revise the copy.

42
00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:36.000
Sam: Create a decision log.

43
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:54.000
Sam: Separate commitments from deferrals.

44
00:12:54.000 --> 00:13:12.000
Iris: I will publish it Friday.

45
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:30.000
Sam: Explain why pricing is deferred.

46
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:48.000
Iris: Note performance needs more evidence.

47
00:13:48.000 --> 00:14:06.000
Sam: Check ticket volume after release.

48
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:24.000
Iris: Support will tag relevant tickets.

49
00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:42.000
Sam: Review progress next meeting.

50
00:14:42.000 --> 00:15:00.000
Iris: I will circulate all materials.
